<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's lower house panel OKs telecom bill - paper.</title>
<headline>Brazil's lower house panel OKs telecom bill - paper.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bill regulating Brazil's telecommunications sector was approved by a lower house committee late Tuesday, local newspapers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Twenty-one deputies voted in favor of the General Telecommunications Law, which sets rules for the privatization of the telecommunications industry, Gazeta Mercantil financial newspaper said. The committee had 30 members.</p>
<p>The bill now must go to the full Chamber of Deputies for a vote and then to the Senate. The government hopes the bill to win final approval next month.</p>
<p>-Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412</p>
